# Cloudflare redirect rules for the deployed artefact.
#
# Astro copies this file verbatim from public/ to the root of dist/. On Workers it is
# never served as an asset: it is parsed, and its rules are applied to asset
# responses. Redirects are evaluated before _headers, so a rule here wins over one
# there.
#
# The playground is a single-page application: its client-side routes exist only once
# Blazor is running, so a cold request to one of them must be answered with the
# application shell rather than a 404. The rules below do that, and they are rewrites
# (status 200), not redirects — the visitor's URL has to survive, or the router has
# nothing left to route on when it starts.
#
# Two shapes look correct and are not. Both were measured against `wrangler dev`
# rather than reasoned about, and scripts/verify-output.sh now asserts against both.
#
#   ONE RULE PER DECLARED ROUTE — never a splat over /playground/*.
#
#     /playground/*  /playground/index.html  200
#
#   is discarded outright: "Parsed 0 valid redirect rules — Infinite loop detected in
#   this rule and has been ignored." The host canonicalises /playground/index.html to
#   /playground/, which the splat matches again. Nothing fails loudly; the file
#   parses, the site deploys, and the rule simply does not exist.
#
#   THE TARGET IS THE DIRECTORY — never index.html.
#
#     /playground/not-found  /playground/index.html  200
#
#   does parse as valid, and still fails: it answers 307 to /playground/. That is the
#   same canonicalisation, and it destroys the very URL the rewrite exists to
#   preserve — Blazor boots at its root and the route is gone. Naming /playground/,
#   which is already canonical, answers 200 with the shell and leaves the URL alone.
#
# The root route needs no rule: /playground/ is dist/playground/index.html, which the
# host serves as the directory index.
#
# A route added to the application and forgotten here works in every click-through,
# because the router is already running by then, and 404s only on a cold link — which
# is the version of this bug that reaches a visitor.
/playground/not-found  /playground/  200
